description: Frontend Next.js React TypeScript rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Frontend lives in:

- `frontend/`

Stack:
- Next.js App Router
- React
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS

## React / Next.js Rules

- Use App Router conventions.
- Use `"use client"` only when necessary.
- Prefer server components when possible.
- Use client components only for:
  - state
  - browser APIs
  - events
  - modals
  - forms
- Avoid unnecessary `useEffect`.
- Avoid derived state when not needed.
- Prefer memoization only when justified.
- Avoid hydration issues.
- Write SSR-safe code only.
- Keep components small and reusable.
- Prefer explicit TypeScript types.
- Preserve existing component structure unless there is a clear reason to change it.

## File Organization

- Prefer existing structure.
- Do not move files unless requested.
- If creating new files:
  - place near related feature
  - use clear naming
  - avoid unnecessary nesting

## Frontend API Usage

- Reuse existing fetch helpers/hooks if present.
- Do not invent a new API layer if the project already has one.
- Do not change API contracts unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve existing field names.
- Preserve existing types.
- Treat `null` values as valid unless existing code proves otherwise.
- Money values may come as strings.
- Do not use float math for prices.
- Preserve price precision.